NAME
    wallpaper - show or set the desktop background

SYNOPSIS
    wallpaper [option]... [file]
 
DESCRIPTION
    The desktop background is a plain file, /etc/vnu/wallpaper, that
    the kernel decodes and stretches behind the windows at startup.
    This command reports which picture is in use, or replaces it.

    With no argument, print the bare name of the background the
    desktop is drawing, or `none` while it is still the procedural
    sky. With a file argument, hand the path to the kernel
    (VNU_SYS_wallpaper): the kernel reads the file, decodes it with
    the same px.h decoder picview uses, quantises it to a palette of
    up to 240 of its own colours in the display palette, makes it
    the background and rewrites /etc/vnu/wallpaper with it, so the
    choice survives a restart of the GUI. A candidate that fails to
    decode is refused and changes nothing -- neither the file nor the
    screen.

    BMP, PNG and JPEG pictures of at most 1280x1024 pixels are
    accepted. JPEG is decoded by the same float IDCT picview uses,
    which the kernel borrows the FPU for and hands straight back;
    every other decoder is integer code and does without one.

    The picture lives in the RAM filesystem and is therefore
    forgotten at reboot, where the kernel seeds the shipped desktop
    back into place. That seed is /etc/vnu/wallpaper.default, which
    this command never overwrites -- it is always there to fall back
    on.

    The same pictures can be picked from the desktop: open the
    preferences window (prefs) and use its Wallpaper pane.

OPTIONS
    -l, --list     list the pictures that can be used, one per line,
                   marking the JPEGs the kernel cannot decode, then
                   the shipped desktop
        --help     display this help and exit
        --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS
    0 on success, 1 on a missing file, an unusable picture, an unknown
    option or an unreadable /proc/gfx.

EXAMPLES
    wallpaper -l
        list the candidates
    wallpaper /etc/vnu/pics/sunset.png
        put the sunset on the desktop
    wallpaper /etc/vnu/wallpaper.default
        go back to the desktop VNU ships with

FILES
    /etc/vnu/wallpaper           the background in use
    /etc/vnu/wallpaper.default   the shipped background
    /etc/vnu/pics                the demo picture pack
    /proc/gfx                    reports the background in use

SYSCALLS
    wallpaper   decode and adopt a background picture
